## Executive Summary

A production UI bug where the Browser panel address bar displayed an internal URL-encoded HTML/data URL (`data:text/html,...` or `about:srcdoc`) instead of a clean user-facing address has been **fully diagnosed, resolved, tested, and verified**.

The issue has been completely remediated by introducing `clean_display_url()` sanitization in `src/ui/browser_panel.py`. Internal implementation URLs (`data:`, `about:srcdoc`, `chrome:`, `javascript:`) are automatically sanitized to `about:blank` for address bar display, without breaking underlying web navigation, history, or real web page loading.

---

## 1. Root Cause Analysis

### Mechanism
When `QWebEngineView.setHtml()` is called (for the initial welcome page or error pages), Chromium emits `urlChanged(QUrl)` with internal data URLs (`data:text/html;charset=UTF-8,...` or `about:srcdoc`). 

In `BrowserPanel._on_url_changed(self, url: QUrl)`, the raw URL string (`url.toString()`) was set directly into `self.url_input.setText()`. This exposed internal implementation details to the user inside the address bar.

